Draft PR for huggingface/transformers — not opened. Written against 4.57.6 source
(line numbers from the installed wheel; re-anchor on main before submitting).
Companion to docs/oss/transformers_musicgen_dropout_issue.md.

Title: MusicGen: default `dropout=0.0` to match the released checkpoints, warn when train mode turns dropout on

Summary
- The released MusicGen checkpoints were trained without dropout (audiocraft
  `config/model/lm/default.yaml`: `dropout: 0.`), but `MusicgenDecoderConfig`
  and `MusicgenMelodyDecoderConfig` default `dropout=0.1`, and that default was
  written into every hub config. In `train()` mode the functional dropout at 25
  decoder sites raises the token loss on the model's own tokens from 4.8 to 9.7
  nats (above uniform), so fine-tuning optimises a path `generate()` never uses.
- This PR (1) changes the config default to 0.0, (2) warns once when a MusicGen
  model enters train mode with any non-zero dropout, (3) adds tests. Hub configs
  are fixed in separate hub PRs (`"dropout": 0.0`, `"decoder_start_token_id": 2048`).
- Behaviour change: only for configs constructed without an explicit `dropout`.
  Existing hub checkpoints keep 0.1 until their configs are updated; the new
  warning tells those users what is happening.

